# PINNED MISSING SET -- every field of qa/field-inventory.json that is not yet classified in
# qa/field-coverage.status. RECORDED ON PURPOSE, exactly as qa/method-coverage.missing pins the
# method work queue and testing/a2a-tck/check-baseline.py pins the TCK's per-requirement map: a
# suite whose result is UNCHANGING is still a gate, because the thing a gate has to catch is a
# CHANGE.
#
# crates/busbar/tests/field_coverage.rs asserts the computed MISSING set EQUALS this file, in both
# directions:
#
#   a field here that becomes carried/waived -> red. Delete the line in the SAME commit that lands
#                                               the coverage, so the queue shrinks visibly.
#   a field that regresses into MISSING      -> red, because it is not listed here.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A WAIVER LIST. A line here says "enumerated, and no instrument watches it yet".
# A waiver says "not owed, and here is why" and lives in qa/field-coverage.status with a date and a
# reason. Do not move a line from here to there to make a number go green -- laundering an
# undocumented gap into a waiver is how "lossless" became false in the first place.
#
# WHY IT IS LONG. The audit that produced this gate found its losses in fields that are never read
# and never emitted -- where a mutation test has nothing to break and therefore catches nothing. So
# "the reader looks like it handles that" is not admissible evidence here, and every field whose
# survival no test asserts is listed below rather than assumed.

